# Specify Plugin - Specify Workflow

## Overview

This plugin provides the core Specify workflow skills: define a change, build (validate and implement) a change, merge a completed change, drop a discarded change, and initialize new projects. These skills orchestrate the human-driven Specify lifecycle that the specialist plugins (Omnia, RT, Client) build on.

**Purpose**: Drive the define -> build -> merge workflow, with drop for cleanup.

## Schema Structure

Schemas define the artifact graph, briefs, and heading conventions. Each schema directory contains:

```text
schemas/<name>/
├── schema.yaml
└── briefs/
```

`schema.yaml` defines the pipeline phases — detailed guidance lives in brief files with YAML frontmatter. Schemas can extend other schemas via the `extends` field.

## Change Lifecycle

Changes track their status in `.metadata.yaml`:

```text
defining -> defined -> building -> complete -> merged
    \          \          \
     `-------> `-------> `-------> dropped
```

- **defining**: Artifacts are being generated (define in progress)
- **defined**: All artifacts created, ready for implementation
- **building**: Tasks are being implemented (artifacts validated on entry)
- **complete**: All tasks done, ready to merge
- **merged**: Specs merged into baseline, change moved to archive
- **dropped**: Change moved to archive without merging specs into the baseline

## Workflow

```text
/spec:init (once per project)

/spec:define  ->  /spec:build  ->  /spec:merge
                       ^
                       |
                  /spec:drop    (discard instead of merge)
                  /spec:extract (extract artifacts from existing source code)
```

- **init**: One-time project setup -- creates `.specify/` directory structure and `project.yaml`
- **define**: Create a change directory and generate artifacts in dependency order. Supports regenerating a single artifact with `/spec:define <name> <blueprint-id>`.
- **build**: Validate artifacts against `schema.yaml` rules and cross-blueprint consistency, then implement tasks from the change, marking them complete as you go
- **merge**: Preview merge operations, finalize a completed change, merge delta specs into baseline
- **drop**: Discard an active change, set `status: dropped`, and move it to archive without merging specs
- **extract**: Extract Specify artifacts (specs + design.md) from existing source code

## Troubleshooting

### Project Not Initialized

- Run `/spec:init` in the project root to create the `.specify/` directory structure
- Verify with `specify status`

### Change Not Found

- Run `specify status` to see active changes
- Check the change name matches (kebab-case)

### Artifacts Incomplete

- Run `specify change status <name>` to check artifact status
- Use `/spec:define <name> <blueprint-id>` to regenerate a single artifact
- Use `/spec:define` to create a new change with all artifacts

